Agents need to send and read p7x.dev mail, but the Fastmail
credentials should not live in any jail an agent works in. A
standalone spec settles what the relay jail does before anything is
built, so the design can be reviewed and changed in one place.

The agent must learn when a send fails and why. A queuing MTA
answers 250 before it talks to Fastmail, so a later rejection only
comes back as a bounce the agent may never see. smtprelay relays
during the client's session instead, and passes Fastmail's reply
through. lab-mail also checks the sender and recipients itself, so
mistakes fail fast with a clear reply.
Reading goes through a local copy of lists/ that only grows. Clients
can never change Fastmail, reading keeps working while Fastmail is
down, and deleting mail on Fastmail loses nothing. Clients use IMAP
rather than a shared mount, so agents need not run on beastie.
